#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# spherical_bessel_j

#% text
# `spherical_bessel_j(n, z)` gives the spherical Bessel function j_n(z).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Integer orders give elementary functions of sin(z) and cos(z); other numeric orders sqrt(pi/(2 z)) times the Bessel function of order n + 1/2.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
spherical_bessel_j(0, x)
#% output
#= sin(x)/x

#% cell
spherical_bessel_j(1, x)
#% output
#= sin(x)/x^2 - cos(x)/x

#% cell
spherical_bessel_j(2, 1.5)
#% output
#= 0.12734928368840825

#% text
# At a high order and a small argument the upward recurrence loses every digit, so the power series is used (the value is about 7e-49):

#% cell
spherical_bessel_j(20, 0.0703)
#% output
#= 6.627918330870939e-49

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `bessel_j`, `bessel_y`
